nce: the parse ends there, queue 228)."] [206 4 "// _PyPegen_number_token: a decimal literal over sys.set_int_max_str_digits's limit, which is the run's: the"] [207 4 "// reader records the digits of one past the lowest limit (p[1]) and the error's location"] [217 21 "// a compiler's warning: PyErr_ProgramTextObject's line"] [228 1 "// compileModuleName is 3.15's compile(..., module=NAME) while that compile runs (nil: none): the warnings' module"] [229 1 "// (_PyErr_EmitSyntaxWarning's PyErr_WarnExplicitObject(..., module, NULL); queue 239)"] [232 1 "// emitCompileWarnings is _PyErr_EmitSyntaxWarning for each of the compiler's warnings, in order:"] [233 1 "// warnings.warn_explicit(msg, SyntaxWarning, file, line); a SyntaxWarning a filter turns into an error becomes"] [234 1 "// the SyntaxError of its location, the compile's result."] [280 1 "// isIncomplete reports an interactive statement that needs more lines (codeop's incomplete input):"] [281 1 "// (PY7: a fresh _IncompleteInputError each time, isIncomplete tells it)"] [297 4 "// 3.15 (queue 239): _PyEval_LazyImportName, unless the compiler forced the import eager"] [332 1 "// eagerImportName is IMPORT_NAME's eager import (_PyEval_ImportName): builtins.__import__ called, or the runtime's."] [335 3 "// builtins.__import__ replaced: called as CPython's import_name calls it"] [356 4 "// a mapping's namespace (a dict subclass's, exec's mapping; queue 219): the names stored through it"] [370 1 "// builtinImportFn is the runtime's builtins.__import__."] [373 1 "// isBuiltinImport is whether o is the runtime's builtins.__import__."] [376 1 "// builtinImport is __import__(name, globals=None, locals=None, fromlist=(), level=0)."] [415 1 "// importName is IMPORT_NAME (importlib's __import__): the module named, relative to globals' package by"] [416 1 "// level; with an empty fromlist the top-level package of the name, else the module with fromlist's"] [417 1 "// submodules imported."] [440 3 "// import_ensure_initialized